# Request

# When the branch detection node fits a line to the detected branch, it samples N points
# along that line and requests their world-frame coordinates in a single batch call:
#           -> x_pixels: array of x pixel coordinates of each sampled point;
#           -> y_pixels: array of y pixel coordinates of each sampled point;
#           -> depths:   depth value (in metres) at each pixel, validated before sending.

float64[] x_pixels
float64[] y_pixels
float64[] depths

---

# Response

# Outputs the world-frame coordinates for each input point:
#           -> points: array of points (x, y, z) in the robot base frame;
#           -> size:   number of points returned.

geometry_msgs/Point[] points
int32 size
